From 0a3256fa10a7cd63b7b839487e97671571bcce40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Corrales <deathcamel58@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:59:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ilitek-ili9881c: Add the inMusic panels

Add the five ILI9881C-based 800x1280 MIPI-DSI panels inMusic fits to its
AZ01 devices, such as the Denon DJ Prime GO. The vendor's bootloader
detects which one is fitted and names it in the device tree, so each of
them needs a driver.

The init sequences are the ones the vendor's bootloader programs,
replayed unchanged; the URT UMOH-9522MD-T and the Goldenvision
GVH070HD98H-C-A share one. The bootloader gives all five the same
timing. The DSI flags - video mode with sync pulses and commands sent in
low-power mode - are the vendor kernel's. Only the URT panel's physical
size is known.

Only the URT UMOH-9522MD-T has been tested, on a Prime GO.

The page 1 and page 4 registers are annotated from the ILI9881C
datasheet. Page 3 (GIP) and some page 4 registers are not documented
there, and are marked as such.

Datasheet for these panels can be found at:
https://gtdisplays.com/Download/DriverIC/Ilitek-ILI9881C%20Datasheet.pdf

Upstream-Status: Pending [new panels for an in-tree driver]
